{"episode_id": "0622ff676d21", "dispatch_id": "dispatch-4", "group_id": "group-4", "agent_id": "sub-4", "arbitration_id": null, "candidate_index": null, "instruction_index": 0, "instruction": "You are working in the git repository checked out at /dayjs (the dayjs JavaScript date library). There is a bug in src/plugin/weekYear/index.js. The user's bug report is: 'There is a bug in src/plugin/weekYear/index.js. Once it is fixed, the test `yearStart: 4` should pass; the version of it that checks this is not in the repository, so its name only describes the expected behaviour.'\n\nContext: the weekYear plugin (docs/en/Plugin.md, section 'WeekYear') provides `weekYear`/`isoWeekYear`-style getters/setters and depends on the weekOfYear plugin (src/plugin/weekOfYear/index.js) and src/index.js. `yearStart: 4` refers to a locale/config option where the first week of the year is the one containing January 4th (ISO-8601 style), i.e. the week-year boundary depends on `yearStart`. The test name means that with `yearStart: 4` the week-year calculation must be correct.\n\nYour job:\n1. Read /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js, /dayjs/src/plugin/weekOfYear/index.js, /dayjs/src/index.js (look for yearStart / weekStart / $W / $y / week-related getters), /dayjs/src/constant.js, and /dayjs/test/plugin/weekYear.test.js and /dayjs/test/plugin/weekOfYear.test.js plus docs/en/Plugin.md to understand the intended behavior.\n2. Find the bug (e.g. a wrong comparison/threshold, off-by-one, using the wrong year, ignoring `yearStart`, or a wrong `$W`/`week()` usage) and fix it minimally in src/plugin/weekYear/index.js (only there unless a fix elsewhere is strictly required and breaks nothing).\n3. Do NOT modify any existing test files. Other subagents are concurrently editing src/plugin/timezone/index.js and src/locale/nl.js - do not touch those files.\n4. Verify: run `cd /dayjs && npx jest test/plugin/weekYear.test.js test/plugin/weekOfYear.test.js` and then the full suite `npx jest` to make sur