{"episode_id": "0622ff676d21", "dispatch_id": "dispatch-5", "group_id": "group-5", "agent_id": "sub-5", "arbitration_id": null, "candidate_index": null, "instruction_index": 0, "instruction": "You are working in the git repository checked out at /dayjs (the dayjs JavaScript date library). There is a bug in src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js. The user's bug report is: 'There is a bug in src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js. Once it is fixed, the tests `meridiem locale AM` and `meridiem locale PM` should pass; the versions of them that check this are not in the repository, so their names only describe the expected behaviour.'\n\nContext: the customParseFormat plugin parses strings using format tokens (docs/en/Plugin.md). `meridiem locale AM` / `meridiem locale PM` mean that when parsing with the `A`/`a` token, the locale's `meridiem` function (locale.meridiem(hour, minute, isLowercase) => string, see src/locale/en.js and docs/en/I18n.md) must be used to match the input, and the resulting hour must be adjusted correctly for AM/PM. A likely bug: the plugin ignores the locale's `meridiem` when parsing, or matches case-sensitively, or fails to set/keep the hour (e.g. hour 12 handling for AM/PM).\n\nYour job:\n1. Read /dayjs/src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js, /dayjs/src/locale/en.js, other locales with a custom `meridiem` (e.g. src/locale/zh-cn.js, src/locale/ko.js, src/locale/ar.js), /dayjs/test/plugin/customParseFormat.test.js, and docs/en/Plugin.md / docs/en/I18n.md.\n2. Find the bug and fix it minimally in src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js (only there unless a fix elsewhere is strictly required and breaks nothing).\n3. Do NOT modify any existing test files. Other subagents are concurrently editing src/plugin/timezone/index.js and src/locale/nl.js - do not touch those files.\n4. Verify: run `cd /dayjs && npx jest test/plugin/customParseFormat.test.js` and then the full suite `npx jest` to confirm nothing pre-existing breaks. Also write a scratch jest test OUTSIDE the repo (e.g. /tmp/cpfcheck.test.js run with a jest config whose rootDir is /dayjs and roots include /tmp) with tests named `meridiem locale AM` and `meridiem locale PM` that check parsing of e.g. '2:00 AM'/'2:00 PM' and '12:00 AM'/'12:00 PM' with a locale that defines a custom `meridiem` (e.g. register an inline locale or use an existing one) and assert the parsed hour is correct. Remove any scratch files you create inside the repo.\n\nReport back: the exact bug you found, the diff of your fix, the commands you ran, and their results (which tests pass/fail).", "parent_agent_id": null, "status": "cancelled", "steps_used": 29, "t_start": 1792140824.5979111, "t_end": 1792141654.663744, "report_chars": 41, "files_modified": [], "error": null, "t_stop_requested": null}
